            <div xml:id="d598">

                <pb facs="0748" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.6363 Standard Oil/73: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Persia</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-12-20T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 20,
                                1921—2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>48. Your 81 December 17, 9 A.M.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d598-f1"/></p>
                <p>Department understands that active negotiations are only with Standard. Sinclair
                    representative told Department on December 16 that Thompson had been instructed
                    to take no action at Teheran except to inform Persian Government that Sinclair
                    had made offer to Shuster. Carefully avoid being drawn into any negotiations at
                    Teheran and observe strict impartiality as regards the two companies. See
                    Department’s 42 November 28, 6 P.M.<anchor n="29" xml:id="d598-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
